<article class="env-remark" id="0ENX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ENX">Remark <span data-tag="0ENX">82.7.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a> let $X/B$ be good. Assume $X$ is integral. In this case the <em>function field</em> $R(X)$ of $X$ is defined and is equal to the residue field of $X$ at its generic point. See Spaces over Fields, Definition <a href="/tag/0ENE" data-tag="0ENE">72.4.3</a>. Combining this with Remark <a href="/tag/0EDV" data-tag="0EDV">82.2.3</a> we find that for any $x \in X$ the residue field $\kappa (x)$ is the function field of the unique integral closed subspace $Z \subset X$ whose generic point is $x$. </p>
</article>